 "unspecified": [
  "Selector value typing: `WEFT-SELECTORS.md` \u00a72 says a `value` is a WCB scalar and that timestamps use tag 0x09 'when the runtime value is temporal', but the text grammar has no timestamp literal and does not say whether a decoded `attr_eq` timestamp is accepted. This verifier accepts text, u64, i64, bool, null and timestamp; that choice is not stated in the selector document.",
  "Selector namespace grammar is not restated in `WEFT-SELECTORS.md`; this verifier applies the namespace grammar from `WEFT-CONTEXT-ROOT.md` \u00a73.1.",
  "Context Root `causal` array ordering is defined in `WEFT-CAUSAL.md` \u00a71.1, not in the Context Root record table. A reader that implements only `WEFT-CONTEXT-ROOT.md` cannot validate the array.",
  "KV provenance \u00a73.2 says the `page` map is the mode-12 descriptor 'verbatim' but does not restate its key types or cross-checks. This verifier had to read `WEFT-AI-CODEC.md` \u00a713.2/\u00a713.4 to implement it; the KV document is not self-contained.",
  "`WEFT-PROVENANCE.md` \u00a72 lists the record fields but never says whether an unknown top-level key is rejected. Every other frozen record schema says so explicitly. This verifier rejects one (NonCanonical) and records the choice; the spec should state it.",
  "`WEFT-PROVENANCE.md` \u00a72 shows `inputs[].object` as an optional hint but does not say whether an absent hint is encoded as `null` or by omitting the key. This verifier accepts both forms and does not normalise them.",
  "The frozen hash-domain table in `WEFTCODEC-FORMAT.md` \u00a71.1 omits several domains that code and vectors use, including `weft/checkpoint/manifest/v1`, `weft/index/state/v1`, `weft/pack/*`, `weft/load/*` and `weft/mw2/key/v1`.",
  "`WEFT-TENSOR.md` \u00a73 fixes the logical record key set and error classes, but the `values_hash` preimage for `q8_0`/`q4_0` is defined in \u00a72.1 with a separate scale/zero-point byte concatenation. A logical-record-only reader cannot check the hash without the tensor layer."
 ],
